You are provided with a $7\times7$ grid of squares and nine cards with arrows on them: six square cards (side 1) with a diagonal arrow, and three rectangular cards with arrows along their length: of lengths 1, 2 and 3 (width 1), as shown. Place the cards so that:

(i) the arrows form a continuous route starting at corner $A$ (bottom-left) of the grid and ending at corner $B$ (top-right);

(ii) all of the cards are used;

(iii) the cards do not overlap;

(iv) no part of a card lies outside the grid;

(v) the edges of each card are parallel to the lines of the grid.

(Cards may be turned to point in any direction.)

Seven year old Rudolph 'Blaze' Ingram ran 100 metres in 13.48 seconds. Suppose that:

- the runner who came second took $1\frac14$ times 13.48 seconds;
- the runner who came third took $1\frac12$ times 13.48 seconds;
- the runner who came fourth took $1\frac34$ times 13.48 seconds.

In this case, what is the total of the times taken by the four runners (in seconds)?
